(5190679, 753470, 94876, '<td valign="top">This should''ve scored WAAAAY higher, IMO.  It''s a really nice shot, and personally, captures the theme better than 10 or 15 images above it.  My 2 cents.  I feel you were robbed.</td>', 'This should''ve scored WAAAAY higher, IMO.  It''s a really nice shot, and personally, captures the theme better than 10 or 15 images above it.  My 2 cents.  I feel you were robbed.', '2009-01-14 10:08:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(5190694, 753650, 86447, '<td valign="top">This is MUCH better than the outtake...   Trust your brave hubby!   :)   Congrats!</td>', 'This is MUCH better than the outtake...   Trust your brave hubby!   :)   Congrats!', '2009-01-14 10:17:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(5190700, 752101, 94876, '<td valign="top">This should have done better.</td>', 'This should have done better.', '2009-01-14 10:24:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(5190707, 752193, 94876, '<td valign="top">I just entered my first challenge, as well.  Not this one, but the Life III challenge.  It''s a good and bad feeling, isn''t it?  Glad to get the first one out of the way!  I also shoot Olympus.  Good to see more people doing the same.<br/> <br/>As for the photo, I really liked the idea.  Lighting would have really helped this capture a lot.  You would be surprised at how far $20 can go at Home depot, which is where my current lighting setup came from.  a 300w clamp-on worklight w./ 10" reflector, and a 150w, as well.  You can improvise a diffusion device if it''s too harsh by lighting through fabric. or bouncing the light off a reflective surface before the subject.<br/> <br/>Hope this helps your future entries!<br/> <br/>best<br/>Josh</td>', 'I just entered my first challenge, as well.  Not this one, but the Life III challenge.  It''s a good and bad feeling, isn''t it?  Glad to get the first one out of the way!  I also shoot Olympus.  Good to see more people doing the same. As for the photo, I really liked the idea.  Lighting would have really helped this capture a lot.  You would be surprised at how far $20 can go at Home depot, which is where my current lighting setup came from.  a 300w clamp-on worklight w./ 10" reflector, and a 150w, as well.  You can improvise a diffusion device if it''s too harsh by lighting through fabric. or bouncing the light off a reflective surface before the subject. Hope this helps your future entries! bestJosh', '2009-01-14 10:30:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(5190721, 753433, 8891, '<td valign="top">Hey it''s you<br/>C Fetor,<br/>yellow ribbons is easy...<br/>Sorry couldn''t resist....Big congrats on your first ribbon, Cory!  Hurray!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-01-14 11:37:25.</i></td>', 'Hey it''s youC Fetor,yellow ribbons is easy...Sorry couldn''t resist....Big congrats on your first ribbon, Cory!  Hurray!', '2009-01-14 10:39:28.000000', '2009-01-14 11:37:25.000000', 0),
