(5205030, 753429, 73452, '<td valign="top">This is Kari Ann, greetings from the <b>Critique Club:</b> <br/> <br/><b>composition:</b> the two are positioned nicely in the rule of thirds, no problems here<br/> <br/><b>color:</b> i love black and white family photos, this is no exception<br/> <br/><b>contrast:</b> nice contrast, his shirt kind of gets lost in the background though<br/> <br/><b>focus:</b> focus seems a little off, the womens eyes arent sharp, and the boys face isnt sharp<br/> <br/><b>depth of field:</b> no distracting elements in the background, so good work on that<br/> <br/><b>lighting: </b> the front fill flash is a little harsh ( i presume that was your lighting situation)<br/> <br/><b>other: </b> Cute shot, but these types dont usually fair well in challenges.  These are good, however, to fill up your family album with and cherish for years to come.  And yes, you are very lucky!  I hope to see you around in the challenges, good luck to your future!<br/>If you have any other questions, feel free ot PM me at any time.<br/>-Kari Ann</td>', 'This is Kari Ann, greetings from the Critique Club:  composition: the two are positioned nicely in the rule of thirds, no problems here color: i love black and white family photos, this is no exception contrast: nice contrast, his shirt kind of gets lost in the background though focus: focus seems a little off, the womens eyes arent sharp, and the boys face isnt sharp depth of field: no distracting elements in the background, so good work on that lighting:  the front fill flash is a little harsh ( i presume that was your lighting situation) other:  Cute shot, but these types dont usually fair well in challenges.  These are good, however, to fill up your family album with and cherish for years to come.  And yes, you are very lucky!  I hope to see you around in the challenges, good luck to your future!If you have any other questions, feel free ot PM me at any time.-Kari Ann', '2009-01-19 18:44:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(5205040, 753550, 73452, '<td valign="top">This is Kari Ann, greetings from the <b>Critique Club:</b> <br/> <br/><b>composition:</b> nice use of Rule of thirds, and leading lines lead my eye down the row nicely<br/> <br/><b>color:</b>vibrant colors, a tad strong though.  <br/> <br/><b>contrast:</b> good contrast in a general term<br/> <br/><b>focus:</b> nicely done on the front buddha<br/> <br/><b>depth of field:</b> I really like how you used such a shallow depth of field, its refreshing.  And that last buddha is awesome, almost like a cluster of stars<br/> <br/><b>lighting: </b>Way too harsh for a still life. Try diffusing the light or finding an alternative light source for better results<br/> <br/><b>other: </b> In technical terms, its a bit of a miss.  The colors are oversaturated, and the lighting is glaring.  But, from a sensical point of view, its very interesting.   I keep a buddha by my computer desk, for extra luck when editing photos. :-D.  I hope to see your portfolio grow in the coming months here at DPC, you certainly live in a place where photographic opportunities await.  If you have any other questions or concerns, feel free to PM me anytime.<br/>-Kari Ann</td>', 'This is Kari Ann, greetings from the Critique Club:  composition: nice use of Rule of thirds, and leading lines lead my eye down the row nicely color:vibrant colors, a tad strong though.   contrast: good contrast in a general term focus: nicely done on the front buddha depth of field: I really like how you used such a shallow depth of field, its refreshing.  And that last buddha is awesome, almost like a cluster of stars lighting: Way too harsh for a still life. Try diffusing the light or finding an alternative light source for better results other:  In technical terms, its a bit of a miss.  The colors are oversaturated, and the lighting is glaring.  But, from a sensical point of view, its very interesting.   I keep a buddha by my computer desk, for extra luck when editing photos. :-D.  I hope to see your portfolio grow in the coming months here at DPC, you certainly live in a place where photographic opportunities await.  If you have any other questions or concerns, feel free to PM me anytime.-Kari Ann', '2009-01-19 18:50:33.000000', NULL, 0),
