(6165699, 752789, 61138, '<td valign="top">To answer hojop25''s query...<br/> <br/>This bird, and many like him, inhabit a trail near where I used to live. So many people hike the trail and walk their dogs there, the birds have become quite tame and will eat seeds right out of the hand. I bought a large bag of seed at a local pet store and I always have a small bag of it with my camera equipment.<br/> <br/>This image was shot in winter when the birds are especially eager to take food they don''t have to forage for.<br/> <br/>I also find that the best shots, especially wildlife/insects/etc. come from spending a lot of time in one spot. Animals get used to you hanging around if you don''t move too much or make a lot of noise. Patience is rewarded.<br/></td>', 'To answer hojop25''s query... This bird, and many like him, inhabit a trail near where I used to live. So many people hike the trail and walk their dogs there, the birds have become quite tame and will eat seeds right out of the hand. I bought a large bag of seed at a local pet store and I always have a small bag of it with my camera equipment. This image was shot in winter when the birds are especially eager to take food they don''t have to forage for. I also find that the best shots, especially wildlife/insects/etc. come from spending a lot of time in one spot. Animals get used to you hanging around if you don''t move too much or make a lot of noise. Patience is rewarded.', '2010-09-18 23:11:41.000000', NULL, 0),
